/timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/get-your-own-party-in-order-aap-targets-rahul-over-state-prez-pargats-remarks-on-anti-drug-drive/articleshow/134973416.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T22:59:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134973431,imgsize-69324.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Will stand with Pakistan if US attacks’: Rajasthan BJP chief’s remark sparks Congress backlash]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/will-stand-with-pakistan-if-us-attacks-rajasthan-bjp-chiefs-remark-sparks-congress-backlash/articleshow/134972702.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134972702.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Rajasthan BJP president Madan Rathore stated that India would align with Pakistan in a potential US-Pakistan conflict. This statement has drawn significant criticism from Congress leaders, including Shama Mohamed. Mohamed questioned the BJP's stance and asked for clarification from Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Amit Shah. Rathore also accused Rahul Gandhi of inciting unrest and mentioned foreign interference in India's stability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/will-stand-with-pakistan-if-us-attacks-rajasthan-bjp-chiefs-remark-sparks-congress-backlash/articleshow/134972702.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/will-stand-with-pakistan-if-us-attacks-rajasthan-bjp-chiefs-remark-sparks-congress-backlash/articleshow/134972702.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T22:35:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pallavi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134972794,imgsize-100936.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[SC Bar Association files criminal contempt plea against Sanjay Raut, Nikhil Wagle]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-bar-association-files-criminal-contempt-plea-against-sanjay-raut-nikhil-wagle/articleshow/134971540.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134971540.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Attorney General R Venkataramani has since granted consent to initiate criminal contempt proceedings against the two under the Contempt of Courts Act. The statements came after Chief Justice of India (CJI) declined a request last week from a delegation of opposition parties to meet him in person. The CJI said the delegation could instead file a petition before the court.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-bar-association-files-criminal-contempt-plea-against-sanjay-raut-nikhil-wagle/articleshow/134971540.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-bar-association-files-criminal-contempt-plea-against-sanjay-raut-nikhil-wagle/articleshow/134971540.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T21:51:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134971840,imgsize-81128.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Her misconceptions’: India rejects US Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal’s remarks on voter rolls]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/her-misconceptions-indian-envoy-vinay-kwatra-rejects-us-congresswoman-pramila-jayapals-remarks-on-voter-rolls/articleshow/134971588.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134971588.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/her-misconceptions-indian-envoy-vinay-kwatra-rejects-us-congresswoman-pramila-jayapals-remarks-on-voter-rolls/articleshow/134971588.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/her-misconceptions-indian-envoy-vinay-kwatra-rejects-us-congresswoman-pramila-jayapals-remarks-on-voter-rolls/articleshow/134971588.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T21:45:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134971733,imgsize-80749.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[IGL rolls out AI system to check CNG cylinder safety at pumps]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/igl-rolls-out-ai-system-to-check-cng-cylinder-safety-at-pumps/articleshow/134971405.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134971405.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Indraprastha Gas Ltd has implemented an AI-enabled vehicle recognition system at various CNG stations in Delhi. This technology checks the hydrotest status of CNG cylinders to enhance safety measures. It ensures that vehicles with invalid certifications are alerted and refuelling is halted. The initiative follows a cylinder blast incident, prompting stricter enforcement of safety norms. The system will soon be deployed at all CNG stations managed by IGL.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/igl-rolls-out-ai-system-to-check-cng-cylinder-safety-at-pumps/articleshow/134971405.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/igl-rolls-out-ai-system-to-check-cng-cylinder-safety-at-pumps/articleshow/134971405.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T21:24:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Atul Mathur</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134971448,imgsize-1231582.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Renewable energy expansion needs to be aligned with transmission readiness: Experts]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/re-expansion-needs-to-be-aligned-with-transmission-readiness-experts/articleshow/134971380.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134971380.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/re-expansion-needs-to-be-aligned-with-transmission-readiness-experts/articleshow/134971380.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/re-expansion-needs-to-be-aligned-with-transmission-readiness-experts/articleshow/134971380.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T21:23:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Atul Mathur</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134971425,imgsize-91002.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Is Dhanush ready to make his political debut? Fan club's new avatar sparks buzz]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/is-dhanush-ready-to-make-his-political-debut-fan-clubs-new-avatar-sparks-buzz/articleshow/134971174.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134971174.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Dhanush's fan club has evolved into the Dhanush Narpani Iyakkam, signaling possible political ambitions. The organization plans to set up local welfare units in five assembly constituencies within Coimbatore district. This transition involves the introduction of a new logo and flag, streamlining its identity. Although comparisons with Vijay's political path are inevitable, Dhanush has not made any official announcements regarding his political intentions, fueling speculation about his future moves.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/is-dhanush-ready-to-make-his-political-debut-fan-clubs-new-avatar-sparks-buzz/articleshow/134971174.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/is-dhanush-ready-to-make-his-political-debut-fan-clubs-new-avatar-sparks-buzz/articleshow/134971174.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T21:07:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pallavi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134971207,imgsize-289991.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Families await return of 3 Indians killed in Germany fire; Kerala CM assures help with repatriation]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/families-await-return-of-3-indians-killed-in-germany-fire-kerala-cm-assures-help-with-repatriation/articleshow/134971104.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134971104.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/families-await-return-of-3-indians-killed-in-germany-fire-kerala-cm-assures-help-with-repatriation/articleshow/134971104.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/families-await-return-of-3-indians-killed-in-germany-fire-kerala-cm-assures-help-with-repatriation/articleshow/134971104.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T21:05:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134971182,imgsize-78799.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Delhi Police signals conditional nod for flag-waving, anthem at CJP's Oct 16 march amid curbs]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-police-signals-conditional-nod-for-flag-waving-anthem-at-cjps-oct-16-march-amid-curbs/articleshow/134971017.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134971017.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-police-signals-conditional-nod-for-flag-waving-anthem-at-cjps-oct-16-march-amid-curbs/articleshow/134971017.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-police-signals-conditional-nod-for-flag-waving-anthem-at-cjps-oct-16-march-amid-curbs/articleshow/134971017.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T20:54:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134971082,imgsize-158408.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Amit Shah vows to eliminate every trace of Naxalism after five decades of tribal suffering]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-vows-to-eliminate-every-trace-of-naxalism-after-five-decades-of-tribal-suffering/articleshow/134970426.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134970426.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Amit Shah highlighted the importance of eradicating Naxalism to restore growth in Bastar, Chhattisgarh. He noted that significant efforts had been made in this regard by local tribal leadership. Shah mentioned a distribution program of assistive devices benefiting over 3,600 disabled individuals, particularly Naxal violence victims. He emphasized the need to heal the wounds from years of suffering while maintaining that Naxalism's end does not restore dignity immediately.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-vows-to-eliminate-every-trace-of-naxalism-after-five-decades-of-tribal-suffering/articleshow/134970426.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-vows-to-eliminate-every-trace-of-naxalism-after-five-decades-of-tribal-suffering/articleshow/134970426.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T20:10:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134970454,imgsize-28450.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Supreme Court seeks Centre’s response on plea to hold protest organisers liable for damage]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/supreme-court-seeks-centres-response-on-plea-to-hold-protest-organisers-liable-for-damage/articleshow/134970295.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134970295.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Supreme Court has requested responses regarding a plea to hold protest organizers accountable for damages. This includes potential liabilities for loss of life, injuries, and property damage incurred during protests. Additionally, the plea advocates for designated protest locations to minimize disturbances in densely populated areas. It proposes that protest organizers disclose their funding sources to ensure transparency.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/supreme-court-seeks-centres-response-on-plea-to-hold-protest-organisers-liable-for-damage/articleshow/134970295.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/supreme-court-seeks-centres-response-on-plea-to-hold-protest-organisers-liable-for-damage/articleshow/134970295.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T20:02:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134970373,imgsize-81128.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[J&amp;K HC restricts motorboat operations on Dal Lake]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jk-hc-restricts-motorboat-operations-on-dal-lake/articleshow/134970038.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134970038.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The high court of Jammu and Kashmir and Ladakh has ordered a ban on fuel-powered motorboats and jet skis on Dal Lake. Authorities are directed to enforce this prohibition strictly to protect the lake from pollution. The court suggested exploring solar-powered boats as an alternative for tourism-related activities. Emergency services and safety operations are exempt from this ban. A comprehensive policy on motorised boat operations is expected for further review.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jk-hc-restricts-motorboat-operations-on-dal-lake/articleshow/134970038.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jk-hc-restricts-motorboat-operations-on-dal-lake/articleshow/134970038.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T19:50:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134970210,imgsize-149574.cms"/></item></channel></rss>